        "procedure": "Hpytza (0.0243 g, 0.1 mmol) was dissolved in 0.5 mL distilled water and the pH was adjusted to 7 with KOH (0.2 M). Ethanol (3 mL) and DyCl3·6H2O (0.0355 g, 0.1 mmol) were added. The mixture was sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined stainless-steel container and heated at 130 °C for 48 h. Needle crystals of [Dy4(pytza)5(OH)4(H2O)7Cl]Cl2·4H2O were obtained. Yield: 45% based on Dy3+ consumed.",
